        "id": 1003224
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-09-17T20:10:06Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "i think it\u0027s _really_ important specifically with async crashes --- the reason i was reading this carefully was that bug earlier today where i genuinely don\u0027t know what this means in practice. (\"context switch\" kind of implies it should be on the same thread at least, but since i have multiple _cores_ maybe not? executed on _the core that had the fault_ or executed on _any_ core?)",
      "revId": "80f2f58a9b6528567eca0770394d24c369085021",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "52142f76_a616ecbe",
        "filename": "/COMMIT_MSG",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 9,
      "author": {
        "id": 1005967
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-09-17T20:21:57Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "It is definitely same thread, not same core.\n\nBut since memory is shared between threads, \"memory corruption\" is kind of a process property. It is a lot more likely to be detected on the thread that\u0027s guilty of causing it, of course.",
      "parentUuid": "26c572a5_e3f572f4",
      "revId": "80f2f58a9b6528567eca0770394d24c369085021",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "42f55fb3_2057e933",
        "filename": "/COMMIT_MSG",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 9,
      "author": {
        "id": 1003966
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-09-17T20:30:03Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e But since memory is shared between threads, \"memory corruption\" is kind of a process property. It is a lot more likely to be detected on the thread that\u0027s guilty of causing it, of course.\n\nThis was my thought process too, which is why I choose to delete the language vs having a process vs thread discussion.",
      "parentUuid": "52142f76_a616ecbe",
      "revId": "80f2f58a9b6528567eca0770394d24c369085021",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "989bff01_567aba62",
        "filename": "/COMMIT_MSG",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 9,
      "author": {
        "id": 1003224
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-09-17T20:46:16Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e But since memory is shared between threads, \"memory corruption\" is kind of a process property\n\ndefinitely, but viewing this from the usual perspective of \"i have more bugs than i have time to look at them --- which one gets my attention next?\", \"persuade me to not just let _this_ bug go obsolete while i get on with non-async bugs that are going to point me at the actual code _and_ give me a strong hint as to what the logic error is\". _those_ bugs are great. async bugs are basically \"trash\" bugs [unless you have the upgraded-to-sync bug that followed]?",
      "parentUuid": "52142f76_a616ecbe",
      "revId": "80f2f58a9b6528567eca0770394d24c369085021",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "3a92a503_809c0645",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1003224
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-09-17T20:10:06Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "(more generally, this is one reason why i\u0027m not sure more use of async in eng builds is a good idea --- i feel like it undermines the awesome actionability of asan/hwasan/sync-mte by giving you the kinds of bugs that seem highly unlikely to actually get any traction? \"something went wrong, somewhere before this\" vs \"here\u0027s all the stacks for all the relevant parts of this incident\".)",
      "revId": "80f2f58a9b6528567eca0770394d24c369085021",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "829d1e1c_ec416e5a",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1003966
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-09-17T20:30:03Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I share your concerns with async mode.\n\nfor the \"MTE in -eng\" changes, the devices where we plan on supporting it will be in `sync` or `asymm` mode, not `async` mode. See also b/367730185",
      "parentUuid": "3a92a503_809c0645",
      "revId": "80f2f58a9b6528567eca0770394d24c369085021",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "b61074f7_97be2031",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
